#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
RG-FLARE-VAX integration driver.

This file deliberately REUSES the exact V4/V5 HBM construction code supplied by
the project, then adds two SILIC-inspired reward mechanisms:

A) Reward-calibrated HBM integration
   HBM8 pattern rate remains the anchor. A small external numerical model learns
   how the five HBM-inspired constructs should adjust that anchor within each
   pattern. Memory-split cross-fitting prevents in-sample leakage when building
   reflection memories.

B) Reward-valued reflective memory
   A reflection rule receives an empirical Q-value according to whether its
   correction direction reduces log loss for similar memory-split respondents.
   Retrieval therefore combines similarity, pattern match, LLM memory-quality
   prior, and empirical historical reward.

Optional SILIC-style LLM reward revision:
   The LLM may propose {-1,0,+1} pattern-level weight directions. A proposal is
   accepted ONLY if it improves out-of-fold log loss. This is external reward
   optimization, not LLM fine-tuning, and not sequential IRL.

V4 keeps the original prior-vaccine-history HBM construct.
V5 keeps the original no-prior-vaccine design and excludes non-target vaccines.

The three source scripts are loaded dynamically so the HBM definitions and raw
variable mappings remain exactly aligned with the user's existing V4/V5 code.
"""

